      C: { story: 'A visual inspiration board narrows the definition of "modern" visually, which is useful. But it doesn\'t surface the user context (B2B finance teams), the use case (6-8 hour daily use), or the competitive context (Bloomberg, Tableau). The visual direction may be right but the information architecture could still be completely wrong.', lesson: 'Visual direction and information architecture are two different problems. An inspiration board solves the visual direction problem but not the "what should this actually do" problem.', principle: 'Brief Discovery', principleDetail: 'Inspiration boards are valuable for visual direction alignment but insufficient as discovery tools. Use them after you understand the user, use case, and constraints — not instead of understanding them.' },
