      B: { story: '"We identified that new users were failing at step 3 because X. We redesigned steps 2-4 to address this, based on research finding Y. The key decision was Z — here\'s why we chose it over the alternative." Leadership understands the logic, asks informed questions, and makes decisions quickly.', lesson: 'Problem → solution → rationale is the most persuasive structure for design presentations because it mirrors how good decisions are made. It answers: why does this exist, what does it do, why this way.', principle: 'Design Presentation', principleDetail: 'The design presentation structure: (1) problem (why did we do this?), (2) solution (what did we build?), (3) rationale (why this approach over alternatives?), (4) open questions (what do we still not know?). This structure gives stakeholders everything they need to evaluate the work.' },
